   "**Strikes on rail terminals, ambulance hospitals and river crossings days before winter move the war's aim from the front to the conditions of civilian life** — nine regions, a destroyed ticket hall, medical staff among the injured, Klitschko rationing car traffic; the direct effect is a humanitarian load that grows with the cold; the compound consequence is that the displacement this produces arrives in exactly the European countries now being asked to sign a mobility scheme and fund a reconstruction — so the war's method and Europe's politics are being wired together by the same campaign"
