  "cause": "**The clause that named the cause was not bracketed this time. It was deleted, in public, by a negotiating presidency with a deadline.** On Thursday, three days after an **18-page** first draft, **Australia's** climate minister **Chris Bowen** published a **nine-page** revised cover decision for **COP31** in **Antalya**. Every mention of **coal, oil and gas** is gone. The earlier call \"for accelerated action to phase out fossil fuels\" is gone; so is the reference to the **COP28 Dubai** commitment to transition away from fossil fuels; so is an acknowledgement of the voluntary transition roadmap being developed under **Brazil's** leadership. On finance, the proposed target of **at least $120 billion a year by 2035** for adaptation is gone — last year's pledge to \"pursue efforts to triple\" adaptation finance is retained, and the arithmetic is deferred to talks next year. The presidency's flagship **35 per cent electricity share by 2035** survives, but the language encouraging countries to reach it was softened and the call to \"accelerate clean electrification\" disappeared. What replaced the verb is **carbon capture, utilisation and storage** and carbon removal — which **Greenpeace's** delegation head **Jasper Inventor** said \"opened the door for the fossil fuel industry to keep ramping up production,\" and which some delegations rejected outright. **The document now records the fever and removes the diagnosis.** It expresses \"deep concern\" at the imminent breach of the **1.5 °C** goal and stresses the \"importance\" of the **IPCC** — while a smaller group including **Saudi Arabia** and **India** wants the panel's next assessment delayed to **2029**, past the **2028** global stocktake that dozens of countries want it to inform. **Panama** threatened to block any deal without a cap on global oil production; Bowen said he had not yet seen its letter. Bowen conceded COP31 will be the first summit to acknowledge the world **will not meet** the Paris ambition, and said negotiators were determined it be remembered for calling that unacceptable. **COP31 President Murat Kurum** called the text the **Antalya Declaration**. Consultations ran into the night; the gavel falls today, and overtime is expected. The summit is unfolding against a record **El Niño**, disasters from Europe to Nepal, and the energy shock of the Iran war.",
  "bullets": [
   "**A text that names the temperature and deletes the fuel makes the cause formally unattributable** — deep concern at 1.5 °C, no mention of coal, oil or gas, nine pages where there were eighteen; the direct effect is that no country can be measured against a shared description of what is heating the planet; the compound consequence is that national pledges become self-scored, and a ratchet with no common unit ratchets nothing — it only convenes",
   "**Substituting carbon capture for the phase-out verb converts a deadline into a technology option, and options can be held indefinitely** — CCUS and removal language in, \"accelerate clean electrification\" out, some delegations rejecting a capture ramp-up; the direct effect is that the operative sentence now describes a method rather than a date; the compound consequence is that the method is owned by the incumbents it is meant to displace, so the paragraph protects market share while reading as mitigation — and removals that are promised rather than delivered cannot be distinguished from production that continues",
   "**Dropping the $120 billion figure while keeping \"pursue efforts to triple\" moves the number from a commitment to a topic** — the target removed, the arithmetic deferred to next year, rich countries citing budget constraints and demanding that China contribute; the direct effect is that adaptation funding reverts to pledge cycles; the compound consequence is that the loss-and-damage architecture is financed by annual discretion, so the countries with the least capacity to absorb climate damage hold claims that expire every budget season",
   "**The IPCC timetable is the quiet damage, because a stocktake reviewed against stale science ratifies the status quo by default** — 2029 versus 2028, dozens of states against a smaller group, the panel's authority affirmed while its calendar is contested; the direct effect is that the 2028 review may run on older assessments than the science allows; the compound consequence is that the evidence base is decoupled from the moment it is needed, and delay in a scientific calendar is indistinguishable in effect from a decision about ambition",
   "**The length of the document is the honest metric: eighteen pages to nine in three days is a ratchet that runs downward** — two drafts, one presidency holding the pen, a single party able to block, a closing gavel; the direct effect is that consensus is reached by subtraction, because subtraction is the only edit no one vetoes; the compound consequence is that next year's conference opens from a nine-page floor instead of an eighteen-page one, so each cycle's weakest paragraph becomes the baseline the next cycle negotiates down from"
  ],
  "verse": "How you look back on these old times today, which according to your present cognitions and terms were bearing in them blatant misery and boundless unright as well as unbelievable unhumaneness, is how your descendants will one day look back on the past, if they think about your time, your actions which are far from the creational laws, your unintellect and your irrationality, your contempt for humankind, the destruction of the nature, the eradication of many plants, fishes, birds, animals and other creatures and the destruction of the climate.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 379",
  "hinge": "§28:379 does not describe a verdict delivered from outside; it describes **how the record will read**, and it puts \"contempt for humankind\" and \"destruction of the climate\" in the same list — because they are one conduct, not two. A nine-page text that records the breach and deletes the cause is that conduct expressed in the grammar of diplomacy: not denial, but an agreement not to say. The hinge is a change in what the text is **required to contain, and who must be named for removing it**. **First,** the presidency should publish a **blocking annex** — which delegation removed which operative sentence, by name — because anonymity is the subsidy that makes blocking free, and a veto that must be signed is a veto that costs something. **Second,** any party relying on capture and removal must report **tonnes actually removed and paid for**, audited, in the same instrument as its production figures, since a technology option that is never accounted is an exemption with a laboratory attached. **Third,** the IPCC calendar should be **decoupled from the negotiating text** and protected by a procedural decision that cannot be traded paragraph by paragraph — a review that the parties under review can reschedule is not a review. §28:379's standard is not rhetorical: it says your descendants will read this record. A document that halved in length on the way to consensus is already written in a language they will recognise."
