   "**$1.76 trillion on $33 billion of nine-month revenue makes one company a macro variable, and macro variables acquire protections they never legislated** — a valuation inside every broad index, $104 billion of nine-month losses, a Fed minute already flagging opaque AI debt and concentration; the direct effect is that a drawdown of a fifth is several hundred billion dollars of household wealth; the compound consequence is that the sector gains an implicit put — because no government will let an index-concentrated collapse run — and an option granted without being priced is a subsidy paid by everyone who holds the index"
